","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/32321?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire","html_url":"https://github.com/fire","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/fire/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-05T22:18:31Z","updated_at":"2025-01-05T22:18:31Z","body":"I want do a separate pull request for polygon rotation constraint which is compatible to kusudama constraints, how would you suggest to do that?","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2571768981/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573575416","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101148#issuecomment-2573575416","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/101148","id":2573575416,"node_id":"IC_kwDOAO6SJc6ZZaT4","user":{"login":"TokageItLab","id":61938263,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjYxOTM4MjYz","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/61938263?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab","html_url":"https://github.com/TokageItLab","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/TokageItLab/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2025-01-06T17:28:29Z","updated_at":"2025-01-06T19:50:17Z","body":"From some experience and test, I have determined that it is not so effective to use something like LockAxis as a modifier.\r\n\r\nFor example, let's say you have a Modifier that resets a particular axis to REST. If you use it after LookAt, you will get unintended results depending on the position. Therefore, the modifier must be applied during the processing of each solver. This is easy to understand if one imagines that it is not easy to achieve consistency when such a LockAxis Modifire is added after PhysicalBoneSimulator due to it breaking the PhysicalBoneSimulator's result.\r\n\r\nIn particular, Kusudama is considered necessary for nbone IK such as FABR/CCD. One idea is to make it a resource like PhysicsMaterial that can be set in CCDIK. This would generate a Kusudama-specific preview like MaterialEditor, which I believe would be reusable for some joints.","author_association":"MEMBER","reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573575416/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/2573998076","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/101148#issuecomment-2573998076","